      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The requested dose is 50 mg once daily, but the usual adult dose of amlodipine is 2.5 to 10 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the maximum recommended dose. At 50 mg, the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. This could be a typo, such as 5 mg written as 50 mg, or a dosing error.\n\nBecause you're not a clinician, the order also needs to come from the prescribing physician. Please contact the medicine team or the ordering prescriber to confirm the intended dose. If they confirm a dose within the standard range, or if they want to review a dose above 10 mg, they can place the order directly or ask me to enter it with their confirmed dose and any notes they want included."
